  "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}a+1.5b-6=0 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6a-0.4b-1=0 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we  multiply the first equation by $\\frac{2}{5}$ and the second equation by $\\frac{3}{2},$ we will get a $6b$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-6b$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}4a+6b-24=0 \\\\ 9a-6b-15=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $b$-variable and allows us to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+\\cancel{6b}-24 & =0 \\\\ 9a-\\cancel{6b}-15 & =0 \\\\ (4a+9a)+(-24-15) & =0 \\\\ 13a-39 & =0 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $a=3$ into the equation $6a-4b-10=0$ to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(3)-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 18-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 8-4b & =0 \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3$ and $b=2.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b=3+2=5.\n$$",
